sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — MorphoEval overall 68.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py` (overall 68.2/100, down from 93.1 in v2). The remediation replaced the Pass 2 closed-form dissection targets with an emergent radial-growth margin integrator and added a growing 2D cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized lateral veins (every convergence point drains to the midvein in WT, none in cuc2-1) and Hamant-type vein-axis microtubule anisotropy, backed by 2 new machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys), 20 reference- anchored measurements and a 12-check self-test. Doing so exposed that v2's 6-genotype r = 0.998 was circular: with one gain calibrated on Arabidopsis WT (0.230 vs 0.228) the mutants emerge smooth (I_D = 0) but Cardamine WT reaches only 0.254 (ref 0.785; sweep ceiling 0.427), mir164a-4 and rco are mis-ordered, and the emergent r is 0.807 (p = 0.052). The margin auxin peaks remain a prescribed template, the benchmark I_D references carry no figure provenance, the specimen \"references\" are the script's own outputs, the mesh teeth sit at the cell-scale resolution limit and the lamina stress-feedback anisotropy is disabled. The specimen segmentation (32 lobes, I_D 0.5202) is unchanged. Overall 68.2/100 (faithfulness 63.6, reproducibility 78.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 72, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/allometric_compound_leaf_comparison.png: rendered output of 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py at d58a084, image/png, 881504 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 4ac058048dd650b246bc2e4bb020b667700ab266be113dacd5722e2e338d3a11 (sha256 4ac058048dd650b246bc2e4bb020b667700ab266be113dacd5722e2e338d3a11), spec_fingerprint f2deb6d5b7f7613348124ac9cf34bbeb431e1d1f13eac9c5772c32d01ccc0fba. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f2deb6d5b7f7613348124ac9cf34bbeb431e1d1f13eac9c5772c32d01ccc0fba; artifact_sha256: 4ac058048dd650b246bc2e4bb020b667700ab266be113dacd5722e2e338d3a11; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/allometric_compound_leaf_reference.json=fa4f9b265dd83379..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/cardamine_hirsuta_compound_leaf_specimen.jpg=1c268fecb3660b31..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/paper_citations.bib=8323f1f35f2613d6..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/scout_manifest.json=46ea1539febdb312...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-allometric-compound-leaf-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429 interconnected leaf margin feedback loops: Loop 1 (CUC2 promotes PIN1 up-the-gradient polarization rho_{ij} propto (1 + gamma_CUC2 C_i) exp(beta A_j)), Loop 2 (Auxin represses CUC2 transcription C_i = C_max / (1 + (A_i/K_A)^n)), Loop 3 (differential normal margin outgrowth v_n(s) = v_0 [A(s)^m/(K_g^m+A(s)^m)] (1 - eta_sinus C(s)) with intercalary tooth insertion) | Vlad et al. (2014) Science 343:780-783 and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) Cell 177:1405-1418: local sinus growth repression by RCO in Cardamine hirsuta converts shallow serrations into deeply incised compound leaflets; growth-based framework with polarity-aligned anisotropic growth | Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109 flux-feedback canalization; Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev 20:1015-1027 marginal convergence points initiate vein strands; Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 / Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 microtubule-aligned anisotropic wall reinforcement; reconstructed_in_script: Prescribed-template margin Auxin/CUC2 profile (convergence peaks are Gaussian inputs, L198-216) with Loop 1 / Loop 2 / Loop 3 algebraic identities verified exactly (Law 1 residual 5.7e-14, Law 2 residual 0.0, Law 3 identity 0.0) and strong Auxin-CUC2 antiphase (r = -0.991) | EMERGENT integrated margin contour (`integrate_margin_outgrowth`, radial proximodistal growth + outward normal term) with emergent radial dissection index: cuc2-1 0.000 (ref 0.012), cuc2-1D 0.000 (ref 0.025), At WT 0.230 (calibration datum 0.228), Ch rco 0.219 (ref 0.312), mir164a-4 0.233 (ref 0.445), Ch WT 0.254 (ref 0.785); 6-genotype Pearson r = 0.807 (p = 0.052, RMSE 0.237); stages P3-P6 I_D 0.000 / 0.168 / 0.219 / 0.256 with 1/3/5/7 peaks; eta x growth-duration sweep ceiling 0.427 | Growing 2D cellular spring-lattice lamina (441 vertices, 804 triangles, bilaterally symmetric) with screened-Poisson growth field, procambial midvein, Mitchison-canalized lateral veins (4/4 At WT, 6/6 Ch WT, 0 cuc2-1 drained to the midvein), vein-axis microtubule anisotropy a_vein = 0.20 (ablation run a = 0): mesh I_D 0.117 (At), 0.131 (Ch), 0.000 (cuc2-1), 0.102 (Ch, MT off); 0 inverted elements; max residual force 1e-3; realised vein-axial stretch ratio 1.04 | Automated excess-green chromatic + Euclidean distance-transform segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Cardamine hirsuta botanical specimen (32 compound leaflet lobes, perimeter dissection ratio 4.0939, radial tip-to-sinus dissection index 0.5202 +- 0.0128 SE) — unchanged from v2; transfer_boundary: 1D prescribed-template epidermal margin signal -> 2D integrated margin contour and 2D growing cellular spring-lattice lamina (reduced-dimensional stand-in for the requested 3D FE vertex mesh); 2D botanical specimen contour morphometrics on a whole rosette canopy, not a single leaf; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element adaxial-abaxial lamina thickness mechanics, cell division, or vascular bundle differentiation inside the rachis | Emergent auxin convergence-point patterning (PIN1 up-the-gradient transport is not solved; tooth number and spacing are inputs) | Reproduction of Cardamine hirsuta leaflet-level dissection (I_D 0.785) or of the mir164a-4 / rco benchmark ordering | Realised cell-scale growth anisotropy from microtubule stress feedback (a_lamina = 0.0 by default; the vein-axis channel yields a 1.04 axial stretch ratio)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py:1250-1338 and datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/allometric_compound_leaf_reference.json:149-154 — the specimen 'reference' values are the script's own outputs. Replace them with an independent annotation (manual leaflet count and per-leaf tip/sinus radii on at least one isolated compound leaf of the specimen, or a second public specimen) and compare the emergent Cardamine WT contour to that single-leaf I_D rather than to the rosette-canopy value.",
            "remediation needed: 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py:187-250 — replace the prescribed `convergence_drive` Gaussian template with a solved Loop 1 PIN1 up-the-gradient transport on the growing margin (the weight identity at L285-297 already exists), so that the number and spacing of auxin convergence points emerge from beta, gamma_CUC2 and the margin length; derive `n_lateral_pairs` from the critical wavelength instead of the per-genotype literals at L546 and L1153-1156, and retire the HONESTY NOTE.",
            "remediation needed: 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py:417-475 and datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/allometric_compound_leaf_reference.json:48-104 — the equal-duration radial growth law saturates at I_D 0.427 (sweep L1186-1215) against the 0.785 Cardamine benchmark. Add the Kierzkowski et al. (2019) / Vlad et al. (2014) mechanism of RCO-prolonged local growth suppression (a time-integrated sinus growth arrest or KNOX/STM-extended leaflet growth window) so leaflet-level dissection can emerge, and at the same time give every `dissection_index_ID_ref` a figure/table/page provenance (digitised outlines with the digitisation script committed) or mark it as a modelling target.",
            "remediation needed: 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py:705-706, 949-997, 1076-1080 — re-enable the lamina stress-feedback anisotropy (`a_lamina`) with a stable (semi-implicit or adaptive-step) relaxation, refine the lattice (h = 0.026 -> ~0.013) so that mesh teeth exceed the one-vertex resolution limit and multi-tooth I_D can be measured without the 2-sample smoothing, and report the realised axial stretch ratio against an isotropic control with a confidence interval." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.682"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 037 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

